<title>EGYPT: Egypt, three firms sign $38 mln in oil, gas deals.</title>
<headline>Egypt, three firms sign $38 mln in oil, gas deals.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt has signed three agreements worth $38.25 million to search for oil and gas in the Western Desert, the Mediterranean area of Matrouh and southern Egypt, an oil ministry statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>It detailed the agreements signed on Sunday as follows and said the companies would also develop any finds.</p>
<p>- An unnamed Tunisian company would spend about $12 million to dig eight exploratory wells in the Western Desert.</p>
<p>- Shell International will spend about $17.25 million to explore for and exploit oil and gas by digging three exploratory wells offshore and onshore in Matrouh.</p>
<p>- U.S. firm Apache Corp will spend $9 million and dig four exploratory wells in Assiut in southern Egypt.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom 20 2 578 3290/1</p>
